[[!meta title="Version 2.03.43 - Feature and Bug Fix Release"]]

Version 2.03.43
===============

* Fix missing phtread key delete. (Regression introduced in 1.02.216)
* Add command line option to edit configuration files.
* dmeventd fixes and improvements.
* Warn on non-power-of-2 thin pool chunk size; prompt when --chunksize is used.
* Wipe stale signatures before formatting a VDO data LV on thin storage.
* Allow stripe size smaller than page size for striped LVs.
* Allow lvchange --refresh and property changes on thin and cache pools' hidden sub LVs.
* Set limits on recursive parsers to prevent stack exhaustion.
* Resolve dmsetup vdostats through device tree and try -vpool name suffix.
    * This allows using dmvdostats on top level device and will report on any
      VDO device it finds underneath.
* Remove cmirrord and clustered mirror log daemon support.
* Respect */run/mdadm/creating-<md_dev_name>* in *69-dm-lvm.rules.*
* Default value of `global/lvmlockd_lock_retries` changed from `3` to `6`.
* Reject undersized --pooldatavdo conversion before allocating pool metadata.
* Many fixes in lvmpersist.

[[!toggleable text="""
See [[!toggle text="more"]]

Editing configuration files on command line
--------------------------------------------

* Add `lvmconfig --edit Section/Field=Value` to set an *lvm.conf* setting.
* Add `lvmconfig --edit Section/Field=-` to remove an *lvm.conf* setting.
* Add `lvmconfig --input FILE` to dump config to stdout or a file.
* Add `backup/config_file_backup_limit` - number of lvm.conf backup files kept.
      Defaults to `50`.

Improvements in dmeventd
-------------------------

* Fix dmeventd raid repair after partial replacement or resync completion.
* Keep snapshot extend threshold unchanged when lvextend fails.
* Retry failed snapshot extension with exponential backoff.
* Unmount full snapshot only on invalid/overflow, not 100% usage alone.

